# =============================================================================
# CI/CD infrastructure - nothing to set by hand
# =============================================================================
# Every fact of the environment (subscriptions, names, networks, runners, the
# registration secret's vault and name, the access scopes, the ports) comes from the
# devops, azure, key_vaults, landing_zone and tags sections of infrastructure.yml.
# Write it:
#
#   pwsh config/variables/scripts/New-IacVariableFiles.ps1 `
#       -InfrastructureFile ./infrastructure.yml -OutputDirectory <folder outside the repository>
#
# That writes terraform/cicd-infra/terraform.tfvars.json and backend.hcl. Keep the
# folder out of git (*.tfvars is git-ignored; a .json file is not). Task 06
# (Deploy-CicdRunners.ps1) builds the same variables from the same keys.
#
#   terraform init -backend-config=backend.hcl
#   terraform plan -var-file=terraform.tfvars.json -out=cicd.tfplan
#
# Each variable is registered in config/variables/schema/master-registry.yaml under
# tools.cicd_infra.terraform_variables. A variable with a default is a setting of this
# code (class c). Do not set a value of the environment in a .tfvars file: a later
# -var-file wins over terraform.tfvars.json. Where the values come from:
#   reachable_tcp_ports                 devops.runner_network.reachable_tcp_ports
#   windows_admin_password_secret_name  devops.runners[].windows_admin_password_secret of the ztp runner
#   additional_role_assignments         devops.runner_access.additional_role_assignments[]
#   tool_versions                       a setting of the code (the module's defaults)
#
# The public key of the Linux runners is not in infrastructure.yml. Pass it in the
# environment:  TF_VAR_admin_ssh_public_key
# Nothing in this file is a secret.
# =============================================================================
